        "original_id": "03ef8184-04da-54ee-b5f3-578d8a8cd84d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Languages: Pashto\n- Communities: Pashtun diaspora\n- Places: Pakistan, Jalalabad, Afghanistan\n- Historical Names: Adinapur\n- People: Hsüan-tsang\n\nFacts:\n- Hsüan-tsang documented Jalalabad by its former name Adinapur in the 7th century.\n- Jalalabad, also written Jalālābād, is a city in eastern Afghanistan.\n- Pashto is the main language among the Pashtun diaspora worldwide.\n- Pakistan is home to the largest Pashtun community.",
